sec.p:
In terms of the effect of aerosol mass, nicotine bioavailability was significantly greater following use of Vype ePen3, which delivers greater aerosol mass, as compared with Vype ePen (Product D (ePen3.0BT18) versus Product C (ePen2.0BT18), respectively, Cmax;
p = 0.0073 and AUC0–120 min;
p = 0.0102). The mean Cmax was 6.36 ng/mL and 4.79 ng/mL, and mean AUC0–120 min was 325 min * ng/mL and 267 min * ng/mL respectively (Table 3 and Fig. 1b). By contrast, aerosol mass delivery by the e-cigarette did not have a significant effect on Tmax.
